       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The FDA-labeled maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). This is about twice that.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum single dose of about 850\u20131000 mg.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe intended order may have been one of these:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Metformin 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- Metformin 1700 mg total per day, divided, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me which dose and frequency to use."
      }
     ],
